In article <DLBRES10.91Apr1133639@pc.usl.edu> dlbres10@pc.usl.edu (Fraering Philip) writes:
>
>Nothing is quite as fun as quaffing to get a Water Demon to get the
>wish, but before you get any of the nifty stuff, a hostile one appears,
>and with only your katana, some shurikens, and (I think ) an orcish
>bow and one or two arrows, managing to kill it.
>
>Something does need to be done about making artifacts a little easier
>to get without wishing while cutting down on wishing in general. It
>seems to me that after a while you are always trying to get wishes in
>order to get the very rare magical devices to win the game.

I really don't see any reason to limit wishing, except perhaps making
it impossible to get a wand of wishing other than the one in the
castle.  Getting a wish from a fountain is rare, *very* rare.
Fountains usually dry out after only a few moves, and each time your
chance of getting a demon is 1 in 30.  And if you get a demon, there
is less than a 20% chance that it will grant you a wish.  Opulent
thrones are very similar about this.  I don't see why it's better to
make artifacts easier to find and limit wishing.  What does it matter
*how* you get what you get?  I think wishing is just probable enough
the way it is, and I'd hate to see it changed.

